{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1221741-prime-one-attainment-reconsidered","id":1221741,"title":"Prime One Attainment reconsidered","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-24T09:54:28-07:00","id":1221741,"title":"Prime One Attainment reconsidered","content":"Mana flows constantly across the world in tiny, unnoticed wisps, gathering into ley line which feed into Hallows. One of the first things a student of the Prime Arcanum learns is that is it possible to gather those wisps, collect them slowly, and over time, replenish one's internal reserves. This Attainment allows the mage to regain one point of Mana every (8-Prime) days, to normal maximum.<br /> <br /> I reconsidered the metaphysics of the previous version. I still like the idea of mages having a way to recover their Mana that doesn't depend on Hallows or Scouring (tass is a subset of Hallow), but doesn't make them redundant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 05-24-2018, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T10:03:10-07:00","id":1221745,"title":"","content":"Have you taken a look at Dedications?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T11:57:41-07:00","id":1221784,"title":"","content":"What are dedications? I find no references them in the core, which is all I have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T12:40:40-07:00","id":1221801,"title":"","content":"I think he may have meant Oblations? (Maybe?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T13:03:36-07:00","id":1221808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1221741-prime-one-attainment-reconsidered?p=1221784#post1221784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are dedications? I find no references them in the core, which is all I have.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure they were in Tome of the Watchtowers. They're an oath (Non-Fate variety in the sense that you don't need Fate to make them) to maintain a particular pattern of behavior and doing so provides a certain amount of mana in return. I can't remember the specifics though. On the bright side, they're apparently going to be revisited and updated in Signs of Sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T13:22:06-07:00","id":1221819,"title":"","content":"From the Edge of Darkness wiki:<br /> <span style=\"color:#949494\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The rules for dedications are simple: When the mage upholds his vow for one week it is considered Dedicated and he gains one <a href=\"http://nwod.org/wiki/index.php/Mana\" target=\"_blank\">Mana</a>. If he breaks his vow at any point while it is Dedicated, he loses one Mana and breaks the vow\u2019s dedication. Note that the mage not only fails to gain Mana from the broken vow, but actually loses one Mana from his current pool.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#949494\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">A vow is either Dedicated or not, it\u2019s not a matter of degrees. A vow cannot be abandoned \u2014 once it is Dedicated it is maintained (supplying one Mana per week) until broken (costing one Mana). A mage can\u2019t give up his vow without the accompanying loss of <a href=\"http://nwod.org/wiki/index.php/Mana\" target=\"_blank\">Mana</a><sup><a href=\"http://nwod.org/wiki/index.php/Dedication#cite_note-3\" target=\"_blank\">[4]</a></sup>.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#949494\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Once a vow is broken, the mage does not lose more Mana for actions against his vow \u2014 he cannot violate a vow that is not being maintained. He does not lose <a href=\"http://nwod.org/wiki/index.php/Mana\" target=\"_blank\">Mana</a> again until he has successfully maintained his vow for another week, after which a break from the vow costs him the Mana he just earned<sup><a href=\"http://nwod.org/wiki/index.php/Dedication#cite_note-4\" target=\"_blank\">[5]</a></sup>.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#949494\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The seven-day period necessary to Dedicate and maintain a vow can begin at any time, though many vow-takers select a customary time such as 12:01 a.m. or the hour of their Awakening. The character gains one Mana at that moment each week as long as the dedication is maintained. Thus the mage who begins his one-week fast at one minute past midnight on Sunday gains one Mana at one minute past midnight on the following Sunday. The mage who\u2019s vow of sobriety began when he woke up in a hospital bed at three o\u2019clock on a Saturday afternoon gains one Mana Saturday afternoons at three o\u2019clock</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T14:52:44-07:00","id":1221849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1221741-prime-one-attainment-reconsidered#post1221741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mana flows constantly across the world in tiny, unnoticed wisps, gathering into ley line which feed into Hallows. One of the first things a student of the Prime Arcanum learns is that is it possible to gather those wisps, collect them slowly, and over time, replenish one's internal reserves. This Attainment allows the mage to regain one point of Mana every (8-Prime) days, to normal maximum.<br /> <br /> I reconsidered the metaphysics of the previous version. I still like the idea of mages having a way to recover their Mana that doesn't depend on Hallows or Scouring (tass is a subset of Hallow), but doesn't make them redundant.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd move it up to Prime 2 - that is where Utility Attainments are located.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T16:04:28-07:00","id":1221865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1221741-prime-one-attainment-reconsidered?p=1221849#post1221849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd move it up to Prime 2 - that is where Utility Attainments are located.</div> </div> </div> </div>That works for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}